calculatePaymentAmount.t.sol
├── when calculating payment for small reward purchases with sufficient value
│   ├── given reward token price is $1.00
│   ├── given payment token price is $1.00  
│   ├── when user purchases enough to survive discount truncation
│   └── it should result in non-zero payment
├── when calculating payment for normal reward purchases (1 token)
│   ├── given reward token price is $2.50
│   ├── given payment token price is $1.00
│   ├── when user has valid merkle proof with 25% discount
│   └── it should calculate correct payment amount with rounding
├── when calculating payment with high discount
│   ├── given both token prices are $1.00
│   ├── when user has 25% discount from merkle tree
│   └── it should reduce payment amount accordingly
├── when fuzzing payment calculation parameters
│   ├── given reasonable reward purchase amounts (0.001 to 1 token)
│   ├── given reasonable token prices ($0.1 to $100)
│   ├── when user has valid merkle proof
│   └── it should result in non-zero payment for reasonable scenarios
├── when testing the zero payment edge case
│   ├── given minimal purchase amount (1 wei)
│   ├── given standard token prices ($1.00)
│   ├── when discount causes truncation to zero
│   └── it should allow zero payment (documented behavior)
└── when testing rounding prevents underpayment
    ├── given slightly mismatched token prices
    ├── when user purchases normal amount
    └── it should round up to protect protocol from underpayment
